WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.410
The Arabic word jihad comes
from a root meaning to strive,

2
00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:06.030
to make an effort.

3
00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:09.400
Muslims speak of striving
with the tongue and the pen,

4
00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:12.220
with wealth, and in armed struggle.

5
00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:16.200
And one more: the struggle
against your own self.

6
00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:19.940
Muslim tradition calls the
armed struggle the lesser jihad,

7
00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.740
and the struggle with
the self the greater.

8
00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:27.050
Why would fighting your own
selfishness rank above the battlefield?

9
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:31.100
In this mission, you'll climb three states
of the self that Muslims find in the

10
00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:32.170
Qur'an.

11
00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:36.390
Then you'll test armed jihad against the
strict conditions that Muslim scholars

12
00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:37.700
set for it.

13
00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:43.000
Your mission: explain why the struggle
with the self is called the greater jihad.
